  "method": {
    "contact_review": "Direct visual inspection of all 15 saved PyMuPDF contact sheets, covering PDF pages 1–239 once each, in 4-by-4 page grids. Each page is scaled to a maximum 310-pixel width and labelled with its physical PDF page number.",
    "detailed_review": "Direct visual inspection of the 22 listed full-page Poppler pdftoppm renders at 144 dpi. This includes the cover, scope, contents, fresh verification, selection counts, one-candidate supplement, moving-space correction, reader routes, evidence boundaries, C66 conditional interface, historical diagnostics and portable commands, catalogue beginning/end, and both navigation appendices.",
    "local_review": "Native-resolution crops of PDF pages 236 and 237 were inspected using both Poppler and PyMuPDF after a provisional column-gutter concern. The crops and PDF text coordinates show a clear gutter; no source or PDF correction was needed.",
    "coordinate_system": "All page lists use one-based physical PDF page numbers. Numeric text coordinates use PDF points from the top-left in PyMuPDF.",
    "not_claimed": "This receipt is visual and targeted prose/navigation QA. Contact coverage is not a claim of full-resolution reading of every catalogue line. It is separate from the completed mathematical source review, compiler replay, axiom audits, and the root agent’s companion-link assembly/pixel-preservation check."
  },
  "checked_observations": [
    "The monograph cover is clean; no decorative motif appears at the top right. The established Komorebi P. pseudonym and revised edition/date are readable.",
    "Across the contact review, headings, source tables, code blocks, footers and continuation headers remain within the page area. No clipping, overlapping content, blank glyph boxes or stray cover motifs were observed.",
    "The fresh verification table is legible and distinguishes 423 selected modules / 4,342 catalogued names / 7,672 logical declarations, the separate terminal module / 51 logical declarations, and the separate one-candidate module / one theorem.",
    "Fresh source history distinguishes the initial stopped run, the diagnostic-stopped elaboration failure, two resource-failed full runs, and the final accepted repaired run. The prose discloses compatibility and local proof repairs, five private helper lemmas, forward inclusion, cached external Mathlib objects, and the absence of a fresh additional leanchecker/independent-kernel run.",
    "The one-candidate supplement and moving-space phase correction are typeset legibly with their stated hypotheses. The C66 pages retain the unresolved general realization endpoint and distinguish its one-candidate conditional comparison from the retained all-realizers formal interface.",
    "Literal shell commands on PDF pages 36–37 visibly retain two ASCII hyphens. The excerpt-display policy explicitly documents reversible unsupported-Unicode tokens.",
    "The source catalogue reaches A.423 and its navigation tables remain readable. The original-obligation table distinguishes original obligation 66 from historical all-records row 66, and directs historical 16.2 to C66 with the conditional comparison separately explained.",
    "Excerpt crosswalk page references point to the labelled explanatory subsection starts. For E39, printed page 30 / PDF page 33 starts the H5 explanation; the literal source block continues on printed page 31 / PDF page 34. This matches the source label placement and is not a broken reference."
  ],
